# Cloudflare Workers Assets — files in dist/ that must NOT be uploaded/served.
# These large PNGs are BUILD SOURCES only: gen-covers.mjs / gen-og-cards.mjs /
# process-bz-assets.mjs / build-favicon-set.mjs read them at build time to emit
# the optimized .jpg covers, OG cards, favicons. Users are served the .jpg /
# generated outputs — the multi-MB source PNGs are dead weight in the deploy.
# Keeping them in public/ (so the build scripts still find them) but excluding
# them here trims ~12 MB off every deploy. Paths are relative to the assets dir.
art/cover-st-johns-canon.png
art/cover-galactic-gospel.png
art/cover-panda-desiiignare.png
art/cover-panda-dump.png
art/cover-canopy-dispatch.png
art/cover-panda-desiiignare-v2.png
art/bz-app-icon-source.png
art/bz-icon-source.png

# OG card PNGs (~19 MB): the served OG images are all .jpg (worker meta uses
# /og/*.jpg exclusively — trackOgImage, FALLBACK_OG). These .png are build
# sources for gen-page-og-images.mjs (it reads a .png, writes the .jpg) or stale
# leftovers from the old PNG-based OG system. Never served — exclude from upload.
og/*.png

# Scratch logo experiments written by generate-logo-spray.mjs — never served.
brand/logo-spray*.png

# Media (wav/mp4/stems) is served from R2 via the MEDIA binding + /media/* worker route.
# public/media is gitignored (CI deploys empty); locally it holds ~30G — never upload as assets.
# NOTE: `media/*` (not `media/`) excludes the mirror's CONTENTS while leaving the
# directory itself un-excluded, so the `media/pub/` publish lane below can be
# re-included. A bare `media/` would make git/assets ignore pub/ too.
media/*

# PUBLISH LANE — the R2-outage fallback. Files dropped here ARE uploaded + served
# as static assets, and the /media/* worker route serves them via env.ASSETS when
# R2 is unavailable or missing the object. To ship a video WITHOUT R2: drop the
# mp4 at public/media/pub/<id>.mp4 (optionally public/media/pub/<id>.vtt for
# lyric captions) and set the track's `video: '/media/pub/<id>.mp4'` in src/data.ts.
!media/pub/
